<title>NETHERLANDS: Stork takes over Dutch components firm.</title>
<headline>Stork takes over Dutch components firm.</headline>
<dateline>NAARDEN, Netherlands 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Industrial systems and services group Stork NV said on Thursday it had agreed to take over Stiphout Precisie BV, a Dutch producer of industrial components with annual sales of some 35 million guilders.  </p>
<p>Stork said the acquisition was part of the expansion strategy of its industrial components business unit.</p>
<p>Stiphout Precisie is based in Helmond in the southern Netherlands and also has a branch in Portugal. It employs 90 people.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
